    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2a4fead_7803fb12",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/MacAddress.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-27T07:42:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since 64-bit hardware addresses are in use (e.g., EUI-64), we should say something about length here. Do we want to promise that these addresses will always be 48 bits long? Do we want to provide no guarantees? ...? API council will probably want to have a say here as well, but it seems useful to propose something in this change.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "d6be080dfcde876c26321a8178d6e5c42e3dde13",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2d0f8df_56791f6b",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/MacAddress.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-27T12:33:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So far the input/ouput API of this class are actually agnostic of the length of the address because conversions are only done to and from Strings and byte arrays.\n\nI think we can start by saying MacAddress only works for 48 bit longs, then consider extending it to 64 bits. At least that\u0027s compatible from an api perspective.\n\nAlternatively, we can also keep it @hide a bit longer, and also add support for 64 bit long addresses in a follow up patch.",
      "parentUuid": "a2a4fead_7803fb12",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "d6be080dfcde876c26321a8178d6e5c42e3dde13",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
