    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "364082e2_61324777",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/MacAddress.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 313,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-27T12:33:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This allows to have a single well defined ctor that\u0027s not exposed, with potential additional validation around it in this static method.\n\nThat can also be very useful in certain case for implementing pooling, deduplication of immutable values, or other things that requires controlling which actual reference is returned. Think List.emptyList(), Integer.valueOf(), and similar methods.",
      "parentUuid": "51353db6_1eacf28a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 311,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 313,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "d6be080dfcde876c26321a8178d6e5c42e3dde13",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a5b5e9d_d3fa4a86",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/MacAddress.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 328,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-27T07:42:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure if we can make a public API commitment to using this particular prefix. Maybe just say that this is a random MAC address with at least 24 variable bits?",
